kevin costner's 1990 directorial debut  dances with wolves set the standard for  modern historical epics a big reason for  its success was the talent of the actors  who brought the tragic story to life  let's take a look at what the cast is  doing now including the wolves  themselves  from 1987 to 1993 kevin costner was on  top of the cinematic world crowd  pleasers mixed with prestige projects in  his filmography garnering praise from  critics and big box office receipts  thanks to fans his breakout role of  elliott ness in 1987's the untouchables  snagged him major attention which was  followed by a string of now classic  films including no way out bull durham  field of dreams jfk the bodyguard and a  perfect world tucked in the middle of  those gems is the film that cemented his  legacy dances with wolves which earned  him two oscars a string of flops and  poorly received films followed including  the much derided water world and the  postman which he also directed still  costner kept busy and continued to  please fans in the decades to come with  romantic comedies thrillers and further  gallops into westerns in fact as  patriarch john dutton on paramount's  2018 series yellowstone costner has  managed to find new success in the  western genre  after 20 years on stage and tv the early  1990s brought new fame and acclaim to  mary mcdonald she was twice nominated  for best actress at the academy awards  the first nomination honored her  portrayal of stans with a fist in dances  with wolves while the second arrived two  years later for her performance as may  alice culhane in 1993's passionfish  mcdonald's career continued to flourish  in the years following this surge of  success she's played strong  multi-dimensional female characters on  screens big and small including the  first lady in independence day and fan  favorite president laura roslin on the  beloved sci-fi series battle star  galactica she's also had emmy nominated  guest appearances on er and the closer  as fans of dances with wolves could have  guessed all the way back in 1990  mcdonnell has made a sterling career out  of playing complex women in unique  situations  the world has gifted us two talented  gram greens and both have provided  endless entertainment between them  however the english novelist should not  be confused with the oneida actor who  boasts over 160 credited roles green's  gentle and soulful work as kicking bird  in dances with wolves earned him his one  and only academy award nomination for  best supporting actor unfortunately he  lost out to joe pesci from goodfellas  green did however take home a grammy for  best spoken word album for children in  2000. for the album listen to the  storyteller among his other notable work  are parts in thunderheart maverick the  green mile skins and molly's game which  reunited him with kevin costner  john dunbar finds his spirituality  through literally dancing with wolves  which is of course how he gets his name  two socks was the only wolf character in  the film but he was played by two  different grey timberwolves teddy and  buck teddy did a majority of the work  with buck serving as backup this wasn't  the only time the canine pair would work  together in fact they were practically a  double act the two wolves paired up  again for an episode of star trek the  next generation as well as 1994's the  jungle book buck gained the spotlight  with a small uncredited role in 1994's  lassie with teddy serving as his backup  after enjoying their long hollywood  career the two wolves hung up their  dancing and acting shoes and retired to  california's wolf mountain sanctuary  teddy passed away around 1997 and buck  followed the year after  after watching sam waterston play a  native american in 1979's eagle's wing  omaha tribe member rodney a grant knew  he had to go to la and bring some  authenticity to the film industry after  a few minor roles he broke through to  the big time when he was cast in dances  with wolves as wind in his hair  choline  casting director elizabeth lustig summed  up his appeal nicely he had a great  contrast in his personality between  ferocity and childishness the contrast  between when he smiles and when he's  serious is amazing  not one to rely on hollywood for a  career he also worked as a furniture  mover when dances with wolves hit the  big screen grande has also been very  active promoting various causes close to  his heart including advocacy on behalf  of native american youth and fetal  alcohol syndrome awareness grant has  been busy on screen as well however the  last few decades have seen him appear in  everything from sci-fi projects like  ghosts of mars to dramas like don't come  knocking  floyd redcrow westerman had already  enjoyed a well-established career as a  musician and activist by the time he  appeared in dances with wolves his first  album custer died for your sins was  released in 1969. he went on to  collaborate and tour with the likes of  sting harry belafonte willie nelson  bonnie raitt joni mitchell chris  christopherson and jackson brown as the  open-minded and friendly ten bears his  talents were put on display to a wide  audience numerous other roles followed  usually wise elders or chiefs westerman  stayed busy right up until his death  from leukemia in 2007. he released a new  album a tribute to johnny cash in 2006  and even reunited with kevin costner in  his final screen appearance in the 2008  film swing vote  rose marie cardinal was dubbed tantu by  her grandmother after the insect  repellent they used while picking  blueberries together in her youth that's  not the only thing she gave young tantu  she also blessed her granddaughter with  an appreciation of her cree and metis  ancestry and an interest in acting  cardinal's career began early in life  breaking screen barriers long before  dances with wolves but the film's  success opened even more doors for the  actress cardinal went on to appear in  such hits as legends of the fall smoke  signals and wind river wind river  reunited her with graham green and not  for the first time they've worked  together on over 20 different projects  cardinal has won numerous accolades for  her work she took home the prestigious  earl grey award from the canadian screen  awards in 2017 and was made a member of  the order of canada one of the country's  highest civilian honors in 2009  aboriginal canadian jimmy herman first  got involved in acting when he appeared  in a yellow pages ad he then worked as a  narrator for the native counseling  services of alberta bit by bit and part  by part herman increased his profile as  a performer until he caught his big  break when he was cast as the elder  warrior stone calf in dances with wolves  a career was born that day over the next  17 years hermann worked on over 40  projects including playing a bartender  in john frankenheimer's reindeer games  and appearing in a guest spot on the  x-files for a number of those years  hermann played fur trapper joe gumba on  cbc's north of 60. off-screen he was  very giving of his time for those in  need herman was sober for 30 years but  still attended aa meetings to help those  still working to conquer their addiction  hermann died in 2013 of a heart attack  at the age of 72.  brooklyn-born maury chaikin often played  outsized characters his brief but highly  tense scene in dances with wolves ended  up being one of his most memorable roles  other works of node included parts and  war games my cousin vinnie and a  memorably harvey weinstein-esque  character named harvey weingard on hbo's  entourage in 1994 he won a genie award  for his work as an isolated former rock  star in whale music in another rare lead  part jaken excelled in his portrayal of  the titular new york detective in the  2001-2002 a a series a nero wolf mystery  busy until the very end jaken passed  away in 2010 on his 61st birthday due to  complications of a heart valve infection  in a film without much room for laughter  robert pastorelli definitely brought  some much-needed comic relief to dances  with wolves as costner's flatulent wagon  chauffeur timmons pastorelli brought  further smiles to the small screen  appearing as the title characters ever  present house painter eldon brunecki  from 158 episodes of murphy brown in  1999 pastorelli's girlfriend and the  mother of his child died under  mysterious circumstances authorities  eventually determined that she had  killed herself pastarelli's life and  career deteriorated sharply thereafter  he did manage to form a close friendship  with glenn close and the two appeared in  a pair of tv movies together in 2001 in  2004 pastorelli overdosed and died at  the age of 49. it was eventually  revealed that at the time of his death  he had been a suspect in janovich's  death  nathan lee chasing his horse also known  as nathan chasing horse born on the  rosebud lakota sioux reservation popped  up in a few tv movies after appearing in  dances with wolves things picked up in  the 2000s in the 2005 tv miniseries into  the west he appeared as sleeping bear in  three episodes in 2015 chasing horse ran  afoul of the fort peck reservation and  was banned from ever returning  accusations of quote human trafficking  drug dealing spiritual abuse and  intimidation of tribal members were  cited as motivation for the ban  michael spears made his green debut by  beating out 500 other boys for the role  of playful young tribe member otter in  dances with wolves he has gone on to act  in over 20 projects many in the western  genre he even reunited with fellow  castmates nathan lee chasing his horse  in graham greene in a number of projects  including the acclaimed 2005 tnt series  into the west spears has also worked  alongside his brother eddie the two are  celebrated hand drummers  tony pierce's spivey is the sort of  character you love to hate an army  soldier with a disdain for the native  friendly dunbar and everything he stands  for he makes quite the splash in the  film's final act in real life however he  and costner are friends and appeared  together again in 1992's the bodyguard  where he played whitney houston stalker  pierce has had a decent run of  supporting work playing wise guys and  intense weirdos in such films as for the  boys and big bully opposite rick moranis  more recently he played a crazed  homeless man on ray donovan things have  slowed down significantly for the actor  since then pierce hasn't acted on screen  since 2015.  kirk bald has not only earned high  praise for his acting skills but for his  work as a teacher and coach as well when  balt enters a scene the brash and mouthy  actor's presence is immediately felt his  most memorable role is likely the  beleaguered police officer marvin nash  who is bound to a chair tortured and  ultimately has his ear cut off to the  sound of stuck in the middle with you in  quentin tarantino's reservoir dogs  beyond this balt has appeared on a slew  of popular tv shows including the ever  popular ncis  [Music]  oregon native tom everett played the  salty battle scarred soldier sergeant  pepper and he's built a robust career in  supporting roles since the late 70s in  2000 he reunited with costner for the  cuban missile crisis thriller 13 days  and recently appeared as archbishop  terrazzi on hellstrom in 1971 rca  released his one and only album  porchlight on in oregon  wes duty has quite the resume both on  and off the screen in addition to being  an actor he's a horse trainer stone  carver musician children's author the  founder of bilingual newspaper a vietnam  war veteran and an activist with the  american indian movement his work and  dances with wolves opened the door to a  steady career as an actor on the stage  and in tv and movies including roles in  the last of the mohicans heat mystery  men the new world and the title  character in 1993's geronimo an american  legend in 2019 he received the  governor's award from the academy of  motion pictures arts and sciences  studies shows no signs of slowing down  he recently lent his voice to disney's  soul  kevin costner's eldest offspring annie  costner landed her first role as a child  she filled in stands with a fist's  backstory by playing the heroine's  childhood self annie later went on to  act in two more of her dad's films  waterworld and the postman in 2014 she  co-founded soundoff films a production  company specializing in quote  mission-driven content of all stripes as  part of sound off costner's work  includes an espn 3430 short about a  short-lived 70s coed volleyball league  entitled bump spike  born charles adams clavery charles  rocket first appeared on screen as a  local tv news anchor in colorado and  nashville he then utilized his good  humor and looks to land on saturday  night live for the  1980-1981 season he was a major player  and even managed to snag a seat at the  weekend update desk but after he dropped  the f-bomb on air and clashed with other  actors and producers behind the scenes  he and a few other cast members  including gilbert gottfried were let go  after one season that dismissal did  little to slow him down as rocket  followed it up with roles in dances with  wolves we're charged with apprehending  hostiles and recovering stolen property  earth girls are easy and dumb and dumber  sadly rocket committed suicide in 2005  at the age of 56.  if you or anyone you know is having  suicidal thoughts please call or chat  online with the national suicide  prevention lifeline at  1-800-273-talk 8255  or text home to the crisis text line 741  741
 

